row(33, 2, 'MATERIAL', f'AND HE SAID: THE LORD CAME FROM SINAI AND ROSE FROM SEIR UNTO THEM; HE SHONE FORTH FROM MOUNT PARAN, AND HE CAME FROM THE MYRIADS HOLY, AT HIS RIGHT HAND A FIERY LAW UNTO THEM. {HP(33, 2, (("ויאמר", "יהוה", "מסיני", "בא"), "and he said: the LORD came from Sinai — Moses the speaker, the Name the subject of the verb (the frame\'s first)"), (("וזרח", "משעיר", "למו", "הופיע", "מהר", "פארן"), "and rose from Seir unto them, shone forth from Mount Paran — Habakkuk 3:3\'s twin cited, never read"), (("ואתה", "מרבבת", "קדש"), "and He came from the myriads holy — the store glosses \'and-arrive\' and \'from-abundance\' (the display patch\'s candidates)"), (("מימינו", "אשדת", "למו"), "from His right hand a fiery law unto them — THE KETIV ONE WORD, Ashdoth\'s word at 3:17 and 4:49 (the ink); the qere two words, fire and law"))} {AP(33, 2, (("ואמר", "יי", "מסיני", "אתגלי"), "and he said: the LORD WAS REVEALED from Sinai"), (("וזהור", "יקריה", "משעיר", "אתחזי", "לנא"), "and the splendor of His glory appeared to us from Seir"), (("אתגלי", "בגברתיה", "מטורא", "דפארן"), "revealed in His might from the mountain of Paran"), (("ועמיה", "רבבת", "קדישין"), "and with Him myriads of holy ones — the myriads His company, not His origin"), (("כתב", "ימיניה", "מגו", "אשתא", "אוריתא", "יהב", "לנא"), "the writing of His right hand FROM THE MIDST OF FIRE, THE TORAH HE GAVE US — sixteen Hebrew words rendered by twenty-three"))} THE THEOPHANY AS THE GIVING OF THE TORAH: the four verbs of coming rendered as revelations, the fiery law read as the Torah written by the right hand and given from fire (4:12\'s and 5:4\'s \'out of the midst of the fire\' on the tape); the Sifrei\'s 343:4 makes the four directions of it with Habakkuk\'s Teman the fourth, 343:13-15 the right hand and the fire. The compile: no law — a status row on Sinai\'s giving (the tape\'s Exodus 19-20 entries the run citation). DV33-01. Fresh.')
row(33, 3, 'MATERIAL', f'YEA, HE LOVES THE PEOPLES; ALL HIS HOLY ONES ARE IN YOUR HAND, AND THEY SAT DOWN AT YOUR FEET, EACH RECEIVING OF YOUR WORDS. {HP(33, 3, (("אף", "חבב", "עמים"), "yea, He loves the peoples — the store\'s \'meaning-accession\' for \'yea\' (the display patch\'s candidate, three seats)"), (("כל", "קדשיו", "בידך"), "all His holy ones in Your hand — the second person to the LORD begins"), (("והם", "תכו", "לרגלך", "ישא", "מדברתיך"), "and they sat at Your feet, each bears of Your words"))} {AP(33, 3, (("אף", "חביבנון", "לשבטיא"), "yea, He loved THE TRIBES — the peoples read as Israel\'s tribes"), (("כל", "קדישוהי", "בית", "ישראל"), "all their holy ones, the house of Israel"), (("בגבורא", "אפקנון", "ממצרים"), "with might He brought them out of Egypt — the exodus written into the verse"), (("ואנון", "מדברין", "תחות", "עננך"), "and they were led under Your cloud"), (("נטלין", "על", "מימרך"), "journeying by Your Memra — the Word the guide (Numbers 9:18\'s \'at the commandment of the LORD they journeyed\')"))} ONKELOS WRITING THE MEANING: the peoples are the tribes, the sitting at the feet is the cloud\'s guidance and the journeys by the Word — the tape\'s own wilderness entries as run citations (the cloud at Exodus 13:21, the journeys at Numbers 9:15-23); the Sifrei\'s 344 reads the holy ones as Israel\'s leaders and the souls of the righteous. The compile: a status on Israel\'s love (344:1, 344:4). DV33-02. Fresh.')
row(33, 4, 'MATERIAL', f'MOSES COMMANDED US A LAW, AN INHERITANCE OF THE CONGREGATION OF JACOB. {HP(33, 4, (("תורה", "צוה", "לנו", "משה"), "a law Moses commanded us — ONCE in the Bible (the ink); Moses named in the third person inside his own blessing"), (("מורשה", "קהלת", "יעקב"), "an inheritance of the congregation of Jacob — 345:2\'s revoweling \'betrothed\' (me\'orasah)"))} {AP(33, 4, (("אוריתא", "יהב", "לנא", "משה"), "the Torah Moses GAVE us — \'commanded\' rendered \'gave\'"), (("מסרה", "ירתא", "לכנשת", "יעקב"), "he handed it over, an inheritance to the congregation of Jacob — a verb added: the handing-over"))} THE TORAH AS AN INHERITANCE: Onkelos adds the handing-over (the chain of transmission the Mishnah\'s Avot 1:1 opens with — cited, the compile\'s case); the outside row 48:9 reads \'the congregation of Jacob\' as ALL EQUAL in the Torah (priests, Levites and Israelites unwritten), 345:1-3 as ours alone and as heritage or betrothal. The compile: a status on the Torah\'s ownership (every Israelite an heir — 31:12\'s assembly of men, women and children on the tape). DV33-02. Fresh.')
