row(33, 6, 'MATERIAL', f'LET REUBEN LIVE AND NOT DIE, AND LET HIS MEN BE A NUMBER. {HP(33, 6, (("יחי", "ראובן", "ואל", "ימת"), "let Reuben live and let him not die — the chapter\'s jussives (the morph codes), the vetitive \'let him not\'; ONCE (the ink)"), (("ויהי", "מתיו", "מספר"), "and let his men be a number — \'number\' a noun the parser does not read (no number line in the chapter)"))} {AP(33, 6, (("יחי", "ראובן", "לחיי", "עלמא"), "let Reuben live IN ETERNAL LIFE — alma, the world, its fourth seat in the book (32:7, 32:12, 32:40 before it; 33:27 after)"), (("ומותא", "תנינא", "לא", "ימות"), "AND THE SECOND DEATH HE SHALL NOT DIE — the resurrection\'s verse in the rendering"), (("ויקבלון", "בנוהי", "אחסנתהון", "במנינהון"), "and let his sons receive their inheritance by their number — the number read as the tribe\'s census share"))} REUBEN\'S TWO LIVES: Onkelos reads the jussives into the world to come, as the Sifrei\'s 347:2 (\'and not die — in the world to come\') and 347:4; the outside rows 31:6 (Reuben\'s repentance accepted by Moses here — chapter 6\'s reading) and 329:3 (death and life in one, with 32:39) join the verse to the resurrection; 347:1 explains why Reuben follows \'the tribes together\' — the brothers\' plea for the elder. The compile: a status on Reuben\'s standing (Genesis 35:22 and 49:4 on the tape; 27:20\'s curse of the father\'s wife at 347:3). DV33-03. Fresh.')
