row(33, 11, 'MATERIAL', f'BLESS, LORD, HIS SUBSTANCE, AND ACCEPT THE WORK OF HIS HANDS; SMITE THROUGH THE LOINS OF THEM THAT RISE AGAINST HIM AND OF THEM THAT HATE HIM, THAT THEY RISE NOT AGAIN. {HP(33, 11, (("ברך", "יהוה", "חילו"), "bless, LORD, his substance — the imperative (the second of six)"), (("ופעל", "ידיו", "תרצה"), "and the work of his hands accept"), (("מחץ", "מתנים", "קמיו"), "smite through the loins of them that rise against him — the third imperative; the verse shares no two tokens with any verse (the ink)"), (("ומשנאיו", "מן", "יקומון"), "and of them that hate him, that they rise not"))} {AP(33, 11, (("ברך", "יי", "נכסוהי"), "bless, LORD, his goods"), (("וקרבן", "ידוהי", "תקבל", "ברעוא"), "and THE OFFERING OF HIS HANDS accept with favor — korban\'s ONE seat in the whole book (the ink)"), (("תבר", "חרצא", "דסנאוהי"), "break the loins of his haters"), (("ודבעלי", "דבבוהי", "דלא", "יקומון"), "and of his enemies, that they rise not"))} THE WORK OF THE HANDS AS THE OFFERING: Onkelos reads Levi\'s handiwork as the altar\'s service, the one place the book\'s Aramaic uses the offering\'s noun; the Sifrei\'s 352:1-4 reads the loins as those who dispute the priesthood (Korah, cited) and the Hasmoneans. The compile: a status on the priestly blessing sought (Numbers 6:23-27 on the tape the run citation for \'bless\'). DV33-04. Fresh.')
