row(33, 26, 'MATERIAL', f'THERE IS NONE LIKE THE GOD OF JESHURUN, WHO RIDES UPON THE HEAVEN AS YOUR HELP, AND IN HIS EXCELLENCY ON THE SKIES. {HP(33, 26, (("אין", "כאל", "ישרון"), "there is none like the God of Jeshurun — ONCE; Jeshurun\'s third seat; 343:1\'s close of Moses\' praise"), (("רכב", "שמים", "בעזרך"), "who rides upon the heaven as your help — ONCE"), (("ובגאותו", "שחקים"), "and in His excellency the skies"))} {AP(33, 26, (("לית", "אלה", "כאלהא", "דישראל"), "there is no god like THE GOD OF ISRAEL — Jeshurun rendered Israel (the third of three)"), (("דשכנתיה", "בשמיא", "בסעדך"), "whose Shekhinah is in heaven, as your help — the rider read as the Shekhinah\'s dwelling"), (("ותקפיה", "בשמי", "שמיא"), "and His strength in the heaven of heavens — 10:14\'s phrase"))} NONE LIKE THE GOD OF JESHURUN: the rider of the heaven becomes the Shekhinah in heaven and His strength in the heaven of heavens (10:14 on the tape the run citation); the Sifrei\'s 355:27-30 reads Israel\'s saying \'none like God\' and the nations\' — the reread row 355:27 at RUN 4. The compile: a status on the Name\'s praise (reference). DV33-10. Fresh.')
row(33, 27, 'MATERIAL', f'THE ETERNAL GOD IS A DWELLING PLACE, AND UNDERNEATH ARE THE EVERLASTING ARMS; AND HE DROVE OUT THE ENEMY FROM BEFORE YOU, AND SAID: DESTROY. {HP(33, 27, (("מענה", "אלהי", "קדם"), "a dwelling place is the God of old — ONCE"), (("ומתחת", "זרעת", "עולם"), "and underneath the everlasting arms — ONCE"), (("ויגרש", "מפניך", "אויב"), "and He drove out the enemy from before you — the narrative form (the frame\'s past)"), (("ויאמר", "השמד"), "and He said: destroy — the third \'and he said\' (the LORD the speaker), the sixth imperative, 4:26\'s word"))} {AP(33, 27, (("מדור", "אלהא", "די", "מלקדמין"), "the dwelling of God who is from the beginning"), (("במימריה", "מתעבד", "עלמא"), "BY HIS MEMRA THE WORLD WAS MADE — the everlasting arms read as the Word\'s making of the world; alma\'s fifth seat in the book"), (("ותריך", "מקדמך", "סנאה"), "and He drove out the enemy from before you"), (("ואמר", "שצי"), "and He said: destroy"))} THE ARMS AS THE WORD: Onkelos reads the arms beneath the world as the Memra by which the world was made (Genesis 1 on the tape the run citation — the world\'s making by speech); the command \'destroy\' 7:2\'s and 20:17\'s ban on the tape (the compiled ban\'s runner cited) — the Sifrei\'s 356:1-3 reads the arms as the world\'s stay and the enemy driven as the nations. The compile: the ban\'s imperative a REFERENCE to the compiled span, no new law. DV33-10. Fresh.')
row(33, 28, 'MATERIAL', f'AND ISRAEL DWELLS IN SAFETY, THE FOUNTAIN OF JACOB ALONE, IN A LAND OF CORN AND WINE; YEA, HIS HEAVENS DROP DOWN DEW. {HP(33, 28, (("וישכן", "ישראל", "בטח", "בדד"), "and Israel dwells in safety alone — the narrative form; 32:12\'s \'alone\' the song\'s word"), (("עין", "יעקב"), "the fountain of Jacob — ONCE"), (("אל", "ארץ", "דגן", "ותירוש"), "in a land of corn and wine — 2 Kings 18:32\'s and Isaiah 36:17\'s phrase (the Rabshakeh\'s, cited never read); Isaac\'s \'corn and wine\' defective, this full (the ink)"), (("אף", "שמיו", "יערפו", "טל"), "yea, his heavens drop dew — 32:2\'s dew the twin by sense with no shared token"))} {AP(33, 28, (("ושרא", "ישראל", "לרחצן", "בלחודוהי"), "and Israel dwells in safety alone"), (("כעין", "ברכתא", "דברכנון", "יעקב", "אבוהון"), "AS THE BLESSING WITH WHICH JACOB THEIR FATHER BLESSED THEM — the fountain read as the blessing\'s likeness"), (("לארעא", "עבדא", "עבור", "וחמר"), "in a land producing corn and wine"), (("אף", "שמיא", "דעלויהון", "ישמשנון", "בטלא"), "yea, the heavens above them serve them with dew"))} THE FOUNTAIN IS JACOB\'S BLESSING: Onkelos names Genesis 27:28 (Isaac\'s dew and corn and wine, on the tape — the run citation the rendering itself makes) as the likeness; the Sifrei\'s 356:4-5 reads \'alone\' as 32:12\'s and the fountain as Jacob\'s blessing too (356:5 the reread row at RUN 4); the pointer row 20b owed at 32:2 (the dew) is the readback\'s. The compile: a status on the land\'s security (reference). DV33-11. Fresh.')
row(33, 29, 'MATERIAL', f'HAPPY ARE YOU, O ISRAEL, WHO IS LIKE YOU, A PEOPLE SAVED BY THE LORD, THE SHIELD OF YOUR HELP AND THE SWORD OF YOUR EXCELLENCY; AND YOUR ENEMIES SHALL DWINDLE AWAY BEFORE YOU, AND YOU SHALL TREAD UPON THEIR HIGH PLACES. {HP(33, 29, (("אשריך", "ישראל", "מי", "כמוך"), "happy are you, O Israel, who is like you — \'who is like you\' the one phrase of thirty-nine with seats beside it (the psalms; the ink)"), (("עם", "נושע", "ביהוה"), "a people saved by the LORD — the Name with bet, once in the chapter"), (("מגן", "עזרך", "ואשר", "חרב", "גאותך"), "the shield of your help and the sword of your excellency — Genesis 15:1\'s shield (the ink)"), (("ויכחשו", "איביך", "לך"), "and your enemies shall feign before you"), (("ואתה", "על", "במותימו", "תדרך"), "and you upon their high places shall tread — 32:13\'s high places spelled otherwise (the ink)"))} {AP(33, 29, (("טובך", "ישראל", "לית", "דכותך"), "happy are you, Israel, there is none like you"), (("עמא", "דפרקניה", "מן", "קדם", "יי"), "a people whose redemption is from before the LORD"), (("תקיף", "בסעדך"), "STRONG in your help — takif the third time"), (("ודמן", "קדמוהי", "נצחן", "גברותך"), "and from before Him the victories of your might"), (("ויכדבון", "סנאך", "לך"), "and your haters shall lie to you"), (("ואת", "על", "פריקת", "צוארי", "מלכיהון", "תדרך"), "AND YOU UPON THE NECKS OF THEIR KINGS SHALL TREAD — the high places read as Joshua 10:24\'s necks"))} THE NECKS OF THEIR KINGS: Onkelos and the Sifrei\'s last row (356:14) read the high places as the necks of the five kings at Makkedah (Joshua 10:24 cited, never read) — one teaching in two books; the shield and the sword the LORD\'s (the help and the might from before Him). The compile: the chapter\'s close a status on Israel\'s deliverance (reference; Exodus 15:11\'s \'who is like You\' on the tape the run citation for the formula\'s turn). DV33-11. Fresh.')
